#: ../../source/run-parallel_README.md:24
msgid "parallel(tasks, [callback])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/run-parallel_README.md:26
msgid ""
"Run the `tasks` array of functions in parallel, without waiting until the"
" previous function has completed. If any of the functions pass an error "
"to its callback, the main `callback` is immediately called with the value"
" of the error. Once the `tasks` have completed, the results are passed to"
" the final `callback` as an array."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/run-parallel_README.md:31
msgid ""
"It is also possible to use an object instead of an array. Each property "
"will be run as a function and the results will be passed to the final "
"`callback` as an object instead of an array. This can be a more readable "
"way of handling the results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/run-parallel_README.md:35
msgid "arguments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/run-parallel_README.md:37
msgid ""
"`tasks` - An array or object containing functions to run. Each function "
"is passed a `callback(err, result)` which it must call on completion with"
" an error `err` (which can be `null`) and an optional `result` value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/run-parallel_README.md:40
msgid ""
"`callback(err, results)` - An optional callback to run once all the "
"functions have completed. This function gets a results array (or object) "
"containing all the result arguments passed to the task callbacks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/run-parallel_README.md:44
msgid "example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/run-parallel_README.md:68
msgid ""
"This module is basically equavalent to "
"[`async.parallel`](https://github.com/caolan/async#paralleltasks-"
"callback), but it's handy to just have the one function you need instead "
"of the kitchen sink. Modularity! Especially handy if you're serving to "
"the browser and need to reduce your javascript bundle size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/run-parallel_README.md:74
msgid "Works great in the browser with [browserify](http://browserify.org/)!"
msgstr ""

